            <ArticleTitle>Samarium-153-lexidronam therapy for metastatic bone pain.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>80-1; discussion 81-2</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.3109/15360288.2012.760705</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Multidisciplinary management may offer alternative therapeutic strategies in patients. Bone-seeking radiopharmaceuticals offered alongside traditional approaches to analgesia may be useful in the treatment of metastatic bone pain. A case of metastatic bone pain in which (153)Sm-lexidronam therapy was used is presented. Minimal side effects, as well as a reduction in opioid use (via patient-controlled analgesia), were observed in this case.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
